{"id":"u-a27c894c-85e4-451b-8951-5c1c40abc2c0","src":"community","title":"Maddox Creason ULPPL 5-Day Workout Program","author":"Maddox C.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/gEUHjy-maddox-creason-ulppl-5-day-workout-program","desc":"I wrote this program as a project for my highschool internship. It is a 5 week program focused on building muscle, but limiting fatigue. I chose doing an Upper, Lower, Push, Pull, Legs split because it has the perfect frequency for targeting each muscle group weekly, while also spacing the days out of which you are training those muscles to make sure you’re recovering properly. I chose to do low sets, and low reps and maximum effort to make sure you are getting the most of each and every rep. I want you to go heavy, while also keeping good form to avoid injury. After the 4th week you will have a deload week to get rid of any built up fatigue you have after the 4 weeks. If I were you, after the deload week I would restart the program from the beginning. Try to increase the weight of each exercise by at least 5 pounds every week, or go for an extra rep or two. I made the program for anyone to use, I tried to make it the least time consuming I could, while also making sure you are hitting each muscle group optimally. I have also tested evry single workout in the process of writing this, and not only did they push me, but they were also enjoyable to me. And after the lower days and leg days, I could walk up the stairs 😂. If there are any critiques I would love for you to review the program and offer me any feedback.","level":["Beginner","Novice","Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-12T19:03:27.210Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper","Lower","Push","Pull","Legs"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Pec Deck (Machine)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","